In <CHp2Eo.2nG@usenet.ucs.indiana.edu>, thomas ward hanselman writes:
> Here's a more feasible upgrade from the present display used in nethack.
> Why not write it in 256-color VGA?  It would look a whole lot neater, and 
> would be easier to write than a 3D version.

1) not everyone has a PC
2) not everyone that has a PC is silly enough to run DOS
3) 320x200x256 games stink on large monitors (ie, larger than 14")

In the OO roguelike game that I'm designing, I plan to store
32x32x24-bit icons of the creatures as well as a default character to
use to represent them.  It'll be up to the machine-specific front-end to
decide which to use, and what to do with the icons (ex, scale 'em down
to 16x16, or quantize them to 256 colours, or ignore them).

If you don't like the text-only interface, buy an Atari Falcon030 and
play Warwick Allison's graphical version of NetHack... he put quite a
bit of work into generating the hundreds of icons.

